The use of logarithms for skewed features (e.g., Debt, Income, Debt_Income_divide), meaningful ratios (e.g., Debt/CreditScore, Debt/YearsEmployed), and targeted categorical transformations/crossings (e.g., Citizen, Ethnicity_DriversLicense_cross) enhances predictive capabilities. Normalizations, group ranking, or combining interactions (e.g., Industry × Ethnicity) further refine predictive signals.

